# Refract — Debug and automation surface

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
Refract carries a small debugging and automation surface, `window.__refract`, so
the game can be driven and inspected from code without moving a real pointer or
waiting on real time.

You implement it. Every operation this file specifies is a deliverable, and the
build installs the finished surface on `window.__refract` as soon as the game has
initialized. Every scenario driven from code reaches the game through it, so it is
present and exactly as specified here.

Each operation is a read or a pose of the game's state. Each pose sets one field,
poses one board, reports one pointer event, or moves the clock; `reset` and
`clear` are the exceptions, and each is the whole of a behavior the game already
has. A pose arranges the board, and the game's own targeting, grab rules, limits,
and completion test run from there exactly as they do in play, so a scenario
driven from code behaves exactly like one played by hand.

The surface is inert during normal play, doing nothing until something calls it.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
